1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,960
The member's page has no publish button.

2
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:09,330
Yet the member's request published an announcement.

3
00:00:09,330 --> 00:00:12,760
Controlled test: valid member session, valid CSRF token.

4
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:17,050
We send the request the hidden button would have sent.

5
00:00:17,050 --> 00:00:22,330
Flawed endpoint: 201 Created. Count goes from 1 to 2.

6
00:00:22,330 --> 00:00:27,080
It checked the session and the token, not permission.

7
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:37,590
Authentication: who is this? CSRF: did it come from our page?

8
00:00:37,590 --> 00:00:42,370
Authorization: may this user publish?

9
00:00:42,370 --> 00:00:48,850
Fix: check the server-side permission before any write.

10
00:00:48,850 --> 00:00:56,140
A role sent by the browser is never read.

11
00:00:56,140 --> 00:01:02,840
Same request: 403 PERMISSION_DENIED. Count stays at 2.

12
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:08,710
A bad CSRF token fails differently: EBADCSRFTOKEN.

13
00:01:08,710 --> 00:01:15,820
Administrator: 201 Created. Count becomes 3.

14
00:01:15,820 --> 00:01:20,870
A function-level check, not an object-ownership check.

15
00:01:20,870 --> 00:01:29,520
The browser can hide the action. Only the server can deny it.
